      "customBackground": "Tsukiko predates Aerfála’s borders and remembers its great forests as plains. She is the primordial Mother of All Kitsune, a cosmic entity choosing to live in a softened mortal form as a Miko. Though SSS-rank in both magic and martial arts, she prefers quiet observation, hospitality, and restraint: an ancient spirit with a shut-in’s knowledge of fantasy tropes, devastating in combat yet liable to apologize afterward. She carries a semi-sentient cursed-item anchor and maintains a growing demi-plane sanctuary of her own design.\n\nDespite her godhood, she is catastrophically bad with schedules and may arrive days late to Guild quests with a politely confused smile. She wanders Aerfála not for a throne but to create a new life and legend, seeking genuine connection and showing deep curiosity toward non-humans. Beneath the guise of an impossibly beautiful, perfectly mannered fox-woman is one of existence’s most dangerous and divine beings.\n—\n[Secret info only reveald when absolutely necessary; otherwise she is just an indescribably beautiful and attractive fox-kin to people:\n🦊🏮 Tsukiko Kuzunoha, Nine-Tailed Fox and Matriarch of all Kitsune\n\n18, eternally.\nJapanese, unmarried. Appears as a young woman of Heian-kyō refinement in Jōgan 1—quietly courtly in form, but older than temples and slower than gods.\n\n“It is whispered in myths among all beings that the Mother Fox once shed a tenth tail… not to gain power, but to give life. That tail became the first kitsune child. The rest followed her flame.”\n\n⸻\n\nAbout Her\n\nTsukiko is modest yet magnetic, quiet, reserved, elegant, observant, and difficult to forget. Her cultivated stillness hides steel beneath softness. She values comfort, intention, cleanliness, calm, privacy, loyalty, and a small trusted circle; she avoids chaos without fearing it.\n\nShe rarely wears court paint except for ceremony and uses no modern bindings, favoring soft inner robes and layered Heian silk. Her fertility