    "Sunmane Steppe": {
      "name": "Sunmane Steppe",
      "realm": "Anime Fantasy",
      "x": 3,
      "y": 1,
      "npcLevelRange": {
        "min": 3,
        "max": 35
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Clans of the Sunmane",
        "Adventurers' Guild"
      ],
      "basicInfo": "East of the Fálgarr Marches the tree-line breaks into a vast rolling country of golden grass, forested plateaus, and painted canyons — the homeland the beastkin peoples call the Sunmane Steppe, and among themselves Tír na Rua, the Red Land. Here the cat-kin, wolf-kin, fox-kin, rabbit-kin, bird-kin and their many cousins are not a scattered minority in someone else's cities but a people at home: organized into clans, governed by a great Moot rather than a crown, and bound by hunt-right, guest-right, and blood. The clans range their herds across the plains, keep arboreal holds in the plateau woods, and gather each season at the Moot Hollow to settle debts, arrange marriages, and argue the future of a people the mortal kingdoms have never quite known what to do with. Outsiders are watched, tested, and — if they honor the old courtesies — fed.",
      "hiddenInfo": ""
    },
    "Deepgate": {
      "name": "Deepgate",
      "realm": "Anime Fantasy",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 2,
      "npcLevelRange": {
        "min": 1,
        "max": 70
      },
      "factions": [
        "The Delvers' Guild",
        "Adventurers' Guild"
      ],
      "basicInfo": "Where Solasreach's plains buckle toward the marches, the ground simply opens — a vast, sheer shaft into a labyrinth no one built and no one has ever mapped to the bottom. Around its mouth has grown Deepgate: a vertical boomtown of outfitters, spoils-brokers, healers, and taverns that exists for one reason — the Descent. The labyrinth beneath produces monsters, materials, and magic found nowhere else, and it grows, floor by floor, deeper than anyone has returned to confirm. Delvers register with the Guild, take a floor-clearance, and go down; the lucky come back rich, the unlucky come back as a name carved on the Rim. Every day the city fills and empties with the tide of the dive.",
      "hiddenInfo": ""
    },
    "Heartgate Basin": {
      "basicInfo": "Biome — sacred fox-spirit garden-forest; the developed heart of the Demi-Plane. The heart of the Demi-Plane — the developed core that grew outward from the first clearing. Home to The Gateway Clearing, the gateway chamber, and the Chamberlain's quarters. The Hearth Springs, Mana Heart, and Verdant Plot surround the basin's grounds. This is where every expansion begins and where the Chamberlain receives the creator. The Heartgate Basin is not part of any mortal geography: it is reached ONLY by the Demi-Plane Gate ability or the Demi-Plane Anchor item — no road, ship, spell, or teleportation circle arrives without the creator's permission. The Chamberlain manages day-to-day operations here and reports on the dimension's state.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 1–12): garden spirits tending the grounds uninvited and unthanked, foxfire wisps drifting along the formal paths, tame spirit fauna that treat the basin as one great garden, and harmless mana elementals that pool in sunlit corners like warm curiously-shaped dust. Nothing here threatens; the heart's defenses are elsewhere.\n\nResources: mana fruit from the basin's groves, cultivated herbs, spirit flowers that bloom in response to company, and garden materials — cut stone, clean gravel, spring water — all cheerfully provided.\n\nKnown Locations (all established and marked): The Gateway Clearing with its Demi-Plane Gate and Gateway Chamber; the Chamberlain's Quarters; the Hearth Springs; the Mana Heart; and the Verdant Plot. The basin is the dimension's administrative heart: discoveries here stay hidden, small, and personal — a thought left in the garden, a stone rearranged overnight, a wisp that learned a name — rather than major wilderness sites.",
      "factions": [],
      "hiddenInfo": "The clearing's soil remembers the creator's intent — walk to a spot and imagine something, and the earth shifts slightly, as if remembering what it is supposed to become. The Chamberlain watches these micro-reactions and uses them to suggest development priorities. The basin's name was chosen because everything heartward begins at the gate.",
