      "name": "The Sulfur Flats",
      "radius": 5,
      "region": "Demon Realm",
      "x": -10,
      "y": 15,
      "basicInfo": "A volcanic plain northeast of the citadel where miasma vents break through the surface in geothermal columns. The air tastes of sulfur and ozone. The ground is stable enough to walk on if you know which paths to follow — the crust conceals channels of superheated miasma that an experienced demon can sense and a foolish one can fall into. The flats are the richest miasma deposit in the fief's territory and the reason the citadel was built where it was. They are also why the fief's miasma level can sustain a noble household — the deposits run deep.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The flats are not purely natural. The vent pattern is too regular. Someone arranged the miasma channels centuries ago — possibly the same architect who built the citadel. The arrangement suggests the flats were designed to feed something at the centre, but the centre has been dead for as long as anyone can remember. The Majordomo's partial translation of the foundation inscriptions may explain why.",
