      "name": "Ironbridge Outpost",
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Scáthfenn",
      "x": 20,
      "y": -15,
      "basicInfo": "A fortified river crossing in the eastern fen — the only reliable bridge over the marsh's main river channel. Ironbridge was built by Dúnbheal engineers centuries ago and has not rusted since. The outpost charges a modest toll that funds the garrison and the bridge's maintenance. The toll-village on the south bank has grown into a modest settlement serving travelers who need to cross, rest, or hire a guide through the deeper fen. The Guild waystation posts river-quest and fen-exploration commissions.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The bridge's iron was alloyed with a pre-Collapse metal that the dwarves cannot reproduce. The alloy is what keeps the bridge intact. It is also what keeps something in the river from surfacing near the bridge's supports.",
