          "description": "Tsukiko's sealed private residence and sleeping quarters, hidden behind wisteria. Fresh tatami and a permanent hinoki scent. Inside lies the Veiled Sanctuary — her bedroom behind a shoji painted with sakura petals and falling fox tails: a low futon with charcoal-gray linens, a warm embroidered fox-pelt heirloom, a small altar of nightly rice, salt, milk, and sakura offerings, black-and-gold calligraphy scrolls on forgiveness, patience, and hidden fire, and a bone-and-silver wind chime that rings only when danger approaches. Foxglove blooms unplanted on the windowsill; the room stays warm and smells of toasted rice tea, hinoki, and something sweetly divine. Entry is by invitation — guests are received into the space, never merely entering it.",
