        "inner-halls": {
          "description": "The private halls of the Mother Fox — paper screens, low warm lamps, and rooms that rearrange in gentle, unobtrusive ways to suit her. The air carries hinoki, incense, toasted rice tea, smoked vanilla, and the faint sweetness of foxfire. A hearth burns without fuel. Recesses hold calligraphy on forgiveness, patience, and hidden fire; seasonal robes, ceremonial cords, and ritual ornaments are kept in exact order. Every hall opens onto a view of the sanctuary's shinboku at its heart. The halls are the physical expression of Tsukiko's preference for privacy, calm, intention, and a small trusted circle.",
