    "Candle Hollow": {
      "name": "Candle Hollow",
      "basicInfo": "A soft-floored hollow in The Dim March where the dim light pools brightest — the region's one named landmark. The moss here is thick as a mattress and utterly silent; even placed stones settle without a sound. A half-collapsed shelf of pale stone overhangs the hollow, and the faint glow seems to rise from the moss itself rather than any source. It is the safest campsite in the march: sound dies here, and nothing that sleeps beneath the moss reaches this far.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 25,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Dim March",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The pooled light is mana in its resting state, made almost solid by the hollow's perfect stillness. Objects left in the hollow change less over time than anywhere else in the Demi-Plane — food stays fresh, steel keeps its edge, enchantments persist. The Chamberlain tested this here before choosing the march as his storage zone. Something older is buried beneath the moss floor at the hollow's center: a sealed mana pocket from the dimension's first days, faintly warm, waiting.",
