    "Cairn Line": {
      "name": "Cairn Line",
      "basicInfo": "A quiet row of small stone cairns across The Fade, each standing at the exact point where ground stops being ground — the Chamberlain's careful mapping of the region's end. Beyond the last cairn, color pales, sound gathers a half-step behind, and the hills give way to featureless mist. The cairns are identical: three stones each, unweathered, casting no shadow in the grey light. Walking the line is the only reliable way to hold a direction here.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 15,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Fade",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The cairns are not decoration — they are a measurement. Each one marks where the dimension's intention currently ends, and the line moves a little each season as the Fade thickens or thins. The Chamberlain rebuilds any that drift. Echo spirits avoid the line: something about the marked certainty of the stones repels them. One cairn, the seventh, is sometimes found with a fourth stone on it that matches no stone in the region; it vanishes again by morning.",
      "factions": [],
