    "The Dissolving Hills": {
      "name": "The Dissolving Hills",
      "basicInfo": "The fading upland of The Fade — gentle grey hills that lose color, sound, and certainty as they rise toward the region's edge. Grass here grows grey as frost, trees stand without leaves or with too many, and distances quietly stop agreeing with footsteps. It is not dangerous; it is unfinished. The hills are where the Demi-Plane simply stops deciding what it is.",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 30,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "The Fade",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The hills dissolve because the dimension never finished intending them — each walk through them takes a slightly different shape. Structures have appeared here overnight: a stair to nowhere, a doorway in a hillside, a lantern-lit path that leads back to its own start. Some are echoes of things the creator has seen or dreamed; none persist past a day or two. Mist pearls form where the fog of two different 'versions' of a hill slowly meet.",
      "factions": [],
