    },
    "Dimensional Anchor Point": {
      "name": "Dimensional Anchor Point",
      "basicInfo": "The still center of The Last Edge — an unremarkable stretch of smooth grey ground that is, quietly, the single fixed coordinate from which the entire Demi-Plane is extrapolated. Nothing marks it: no pillar, no sigil, no glow. The light falls without direction, the air does not move, and standing on the exact point feels like standing in the pause between two thoughts. Anyone attuned to dimensional structure who stands here long enough will feel the whole dimension hanging from this one spot like a coat from a single nail.",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 20,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Last Edge",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "This is the most important place in the dimension and the least conspicuous. Destabilizing the anchor point would not collapse the Demi-Plane but set it drifting until it lost connection to the mortal world. The Mana Heart's guardian entity patrols here secretly whenever the creator is absent. Nullstone and fixed-point fragments are found only within a few hundred paces of the point — the ground's absolute stillness condenses them. The geometric formations occasionally found nearby are not buildings or ruins; they are the dimension's structure briefly becoming visible where stillness is deepest.",
      "factions": [],
