      "radius": 3,
      "region": "The Hollow Vale",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The wind never crosses the vale because the terraced slopes were formed as a shelter in intention as much as in shape. A small spring seeps from the south bank through a buried crevice unnoticed by the Chamberlain; its water makes spirit clay set harder. Burrowing spirit rabbits maintain warren-caves here, some chambers long abandoned — their old shelters still lined with moss and waiting. One viewpoint on the eastern slope sees the Hidden Estate directly, though the sight belongs only to those who climb.",
