    "Mana-Density Survey Point": {
      "name": "Mana-Density Survey Point",
      "basicInfo": "A single pale stone standing in the tall grass of The Deep Expanse, ringed by a worn circle where the Chamberlain measures the region's mana density by hand — one of the earliest man-made places in the dimension. The stone is ordinary except that grass refuses to grow within its ring. A small notebook-sized hollow in the stone's base holds the latest readings, chalked in the Chamberlain's precise hand.",
      "x": 15,
      "y": 30,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "The Deep Expanse",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The readings matter more than the region admits: the Expanse's mana density has crept steadily upward since measurement began, as if the reservoir below the prairie is filling faster than the dimension can spend it. A day is coming when the grass will hum loud enough to hear from the Stone Rise. Mana amber forms thickest within a hundred paces of the point. The Chamberlain has never explained the survey to the creator; he treats it as his private promise that the ground will be ready when she is.",
