    "Sunset Hills": {
      "name": "Sunset Hills",
      "basicInfo": "The rolling golden upland of The Southroll — wave after wave of grass-covered hills bathed in perpetual late-afternoon light. Warm soil, low wild herbs, and an air that lulls walkers into unhurried contentment. Every hill crest offers a new unrolling view of gold, and the fireflies begin their disciplined circles as the light deepens toward evening that never quite arrives.",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 30,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "The Southroll",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The perpetual light is sustained low-state mana — the region is the dimension's lifeboat, keeping itself lit for days on residual energy if everything else failed. Hill fox dens concentrate along the northern folds; the foxes neither fear nor welcome visitors but will guide lost walkers home if bribed with sweet grass. Broad Picnic Groves form naturally in the hollows of the hills — circles of shade-trees that appear where no seeds were ever planted, always with a flat stone suitable for laying out food.",
