    "Eastern Clefts": {
      "name": "Eastern Clefts",
      "basicInfo": "The great fissure system of The Rift March — dark stone gorges twisting into the region's east, deep enough that cold blue light seeps upward from their bottoms at night. The rims echo a heartbeat late. Grassland edges carelessly into stone; the West is the Southroll's warmth, the East is depth, shadow, and something that has not decided whether it is scenery or danger. Cave mouths punctuate the cleft walls — most unplumbed, all unmarked.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 25,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "The Rift March",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The clefts descend toward the dimensional boundary itself; at a certain depth, visitors feel they are standing at the bottom of the world. Rift crawlers and cave drakes nest in the upper systems, but the deep systems hold unexplored caverns, monster nests of higher-level predators, and ruins of strange geometry that predate the March — materialized fears wear borrowed shapes. At least one fissure mouth reads as a natural dungeon entrance waiting for an occupant. Blue mana ore veins run along the deepest exposed walls, harvested only by the brave or the careless.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Rift Overlook": {
      "name": "Rift Overlook",
      "basicInfo": "The grassland rim above the Eastern Clefts — a broad stone knoll where the Rift March's last safe ground meets its first true drop. From the overlook, the whole fissure system is visible: layered ridges sculpting downward into blue-lit dark. Wind rises from below at dusk carrying cold mineral air and, occasionally, a sound not quite echo. A low cairn ring marks the safety line; past it the ground breaks without warning.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 15,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Rift March",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The Chamberlain placed the cairn ring himself after two survey trips, but refuses to survey further without an escort — unusual fear for a being that catalogs monsters without hesitation. Blue-flame wisps rise from the clefts to the overlook on windless nights, circling it twice before sinking back: a behavior he logs but cannot explain. From this point, only the uppermost cave mouths are in sight; the true depths begin where the overlook's map ends and every route beyond is discovery, not documentation.",
