      "basicInfo": "A nondescript traveler who shows up in inconvenient places — the Bramblewatch Tower, the Crossroads Inn, the Old Stone Bridge. Rook asks polite questions, buys drinks for strangers, and remembers everything. He is not a fighter, not a merchant, and definitely not a spy. He is also definitely a spy. The Pale Hand uses him as a field observer for the Bréanriv-Fálgarr corridor, and he is very good at his job — good enough that the only people who have identified him are the ones he has decided are harmless. Deliberately forgettable — average height, brown hair, brown eyes, the kind of face that blends into every crowd. He dresses like a journeyman merchant, speaks like a friendly local, and is gone before you realize you never learned his real name. The only distinctive thing about him is his watchfulness — if you catch him when he thinks no one is looking, his eyes are recording everything with the focus of a man who knows that the wrong detail missed is the last detail he sees.",
