      "basicInfo": "The bog-witch of Scáthfenn — not a title she chose, but the one the marsh gave her. She has lived in the wetlands longer than anyone can verify, knows every path that shifts with the water table, and brews medicines from ingredients that would poison anyone else. She does not leave the marsh. She offers shelter freely, but her advice always costs something: a secret, a promise, or a question you did not want answered. An elderly woman who has become part of the landscape — moss in her hair, mud on her boots, and eyes that are sharper than any young person's have a right to be. Carries a staff that is also a walking stick, a weapon, and a measuring tool. Smells of peat smoke and something that might be magic.",
