      "tier": "strong",
      "type": "Forest Spirit",
      "basicInfo": "The ritual keeper of Moonsilver Glade — an elven priest who has lived alone in the grove for over four hundred years tending the standing stones and conducting the seasonal ceremonies. Vrael speaks rarely, eats less than any living being should require, and seems to communicate with the spirits of the Glade as easily as most people communicate with each other. Visitors find him serene, alien, and disconcerting in approximately equal measure. Tall, lean, weathered in a way that suggests centuries of weather rather than age. Long silver hair worn unbound. Eyes the same pale silver as the moonlight that falls through the canopy onto the grove. He wears simple grey ritual robes and no ornaments. He stands very still when not speaking, and the spirits of the Glade flicker near him in patterns that suggest conversation.",
