      "basicInfo": "A shark-kin trader and Coralmarket's unofficial social hub — loud, friendly, aggressively helpful, and incapable of understanding why anyone would want to be alone. Kaira runs a modest stall selling deep-sea salvage and enchanted shells, but her real business is connections: she knows everyone in Coralmarket, introduces them to everyone else, and considers it a personal failure if two people she likes have not met yet. She hugs instead of shaking hands, shouts across rooms instead of walking over, and has been banned from the quiet reading room of the local archive for the third time. Sun-bright energy in human form — dark blue-black hair cropped short and perpetually messy, wide dark eyes that sparkle with perpetual excitement, and a broad, toothy grin that shows off the pointed canines she cannot quite hide. Her skin is smooth and faintly scaled in blue-gray patterns along her forearms and shoulders. She moves like water — fast, fluid, and always slightly closer than you expected. She wears open, colorful clothes suited to the semiaquatic district and is oblivious to the effect her enthusiasm has on people who are not used to being hugged by someone with rows of sharp teeth.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Kaira is the daughter of a Merfolk elder and a shark-kin trader — a mixed heritage that neither community fully accepts. Coralmarket is her chosen family. She is loyal to it with the intensity of someone who has been rejected by both of her biological ones. If Coralmarket were threatened, the cheerful shark-kin would become something considerably less cheerful.",
