      "basicInfo": "A forest spirit who has been bound to the Palebark Ruins for centuries — anchored by a forgotten pact that none of the current forest residents remember making. He cannot leave the ruins. He cannot die. He watches the forest change around him, unable to participate, making conversation with visitors and playing pranks that are more lonely than malicious. To free him, someone must break the anchor — a stone hidden in the ruins. Finding it is the easy part. Breaking it requires someone the spirit would choose to follow. A flickering presence — sometimes a young man made of autumn leaves, sometimes a fox made of moonlight, sometimes just a voice with a laugh in it. When he concentrates, he can hold a form: a slight figure with bark-textured skin and eyes like amber sap. He smells of rain and old wood.",
