      "basicInfo": "The head of the Circle of Elders and Caelvir's de facto head of state — a woman who has led her people for four hundred years with the poise of someone who has already considered every possible objection and found it wanting. Faelwen speaks rarely and precisely; when she looks at you, the rest of the world dims. She is aware of her effect on people and uses it with surgical precision — not for manipulation, but because attention is a resource and she controls where it goes. Her public position is neutrality toward the outside world. Her private position is considerably more complicated. Ethereal — silver-white hair that falls to her waist, violet eyes that hold four centuries of patience, and a face so still and perfect that it reads as carved rather than born. She moves like water over stone: slow, inevitable, and impossible to redirect. Her robes are woven from World-Tree bark fiber and seem to shift color in different light. When she speaks, the forest goes quiet — not from fear, but from the simple fact that whatever she is about to say is probably important.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Faelwen knows the World-Tree is dying. She has known for a decade. She has been feeding it her own life-force to buy time — a secret she keeps because the alternative is civil war among the Elders and a land grab by every faction on the continent. She has maybe five years of life left if she continues. The tree has maybe ten. She is choosing to spend her remaining years making sure the transition — whatever it looks like — does not destroy her people.",
