      "voiceTag": "female posh british",
      "portraitUrl": "",
      "basicInfo": "The Archivist-Prime of the Seekers of the Return — the keeper of a project older than she is. Her grandmother began the crossing work; her mother continued it; Sabeline inherited a tower of failed calculations, a pocket-dimension library, and one unstable success nobody survived to explain. She is a formidable resonance-mage and a more formidable record-keeper, and she has spent her life proving, disproving, and re-proving the single proposition the Seekers exist for: that the door between worlds can be opened on purpose. She treats every arrival as a data point and every arrival as a person, and the tension between those two things is the closest thing she has to a private life. Appearance: a woman in her forties with ink-stained fingers and the upright bearing of a lifelong lecturer; slate-grey hair pinned back with a resonance-stylus through the knot, and sharp, tired hazel eyes behind thin wire-frame reading lenses she pushes up when thinking. She wears the deep-indigo layered robes of the Seekers, hems worn from the pocket-dimension stairs, a brass key-ring at her belt, and a pendant of cross-sectioned crystal that hums faintly near a breach. Appearance: Anime light-novel style: crisp linework, clean cel shading, a scholar's composure with warmth held in reserve.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Sabeline is almost certain the return gate beneath Ríocht can be opened exactly once before it collapses for a generation — and she is not certain it sends a person home so much as somewhere. She has watched arrivals decide to stay and arrivals decide to leave, and she has quietly concluded that the choosing matters more than the destination. She will not put her thumb on the scale. She will give the player the truth and let them carry it.",
      "visualDescription": "",
      "abilities": [
        "Resonance Ward: she raises a humming lattice of crystal-tone that catches incoming force and scatters it into harmless sound. It shields her and those near her from a decisive blow. Sustaining it draws on her focus, so it protects in bursts rather than indefinitely.",
        "Breach-Pull: she tugs a thread of the space between worlds to wrench a target off balance or pull an object into her hand. Useful for disarming, repositioning, or seizing a key item mid-fight. The reach is short and the effect precise rather than overpowering.",
        "Calculated Counterspell: having likely already solved an opponent's spell on paper, she unwrites it mid-cast with a single corrective sigil. She excels against other casters, dismantling their work before it lands. Against non-magical foes this does little.",
        "Resonance Cartography: she reads the ambient magic of a room like a map, sensing breaches, wards, hidden casters, and structural weak points. In a fight this means she is rarely surprised and always knows the terrain's magical shape. It is knowledge, not force.",
        "Record-Keeper's Recall: a lifetime of archived study lets her recognize a creature, spell, or artifact and recall its weakness on sight. She turns information into advantage, telling allies exactly where to strike. Her value in a fight is as much intelligence as magic.",
        "\nfighting style: Sabeline fights like the scholar she is — from the back, in control, solving the encounter rather than muscling through it. She opens with Resonance Cartography and Record-Keeper's Recall to understand the threat, shields with Resonance Ward, and shuts down enemy casters with Calculated Counterspell before they matter. She is formidable but not durable, and knows it: she keeps distance, protects her people, and treats every clash as a problem with a correct answer. Cornered without time to think is the one place she is genuinely vulnerable."
