  "storySettings": {
    "worldBackground": "Aerfála is an anime-fantasy world governed by light-novel logic. Adventurers' Guild branches stand in every major town, posting quests ranked F through S. Magic is colorful, abundant, and color-coded by element. A Demon Lord's Army lurks beyond the frontier, threatening the settled lands. The four great powers — the human Kingdom of Solasreach, the elven Caelvir Forest Commune, the dwarven Kingdom of Dúnbheal, and the multiracial Muirscáth Free Cities — maintain an uneasy peace while adventurers handle the monsters, dungeons, and crises that regular armies cannot. Hot springs are everywhere. So is trouble. Guild ranks determine everything from quest access to social standing, and an adventurer's card is worth more than a noble's signature in most towns. Romance blooms between dungeon dives, rivalries ignite over quest board bounties, and the bathhouse is where half the important conversations happen.",
    "questGenerationGuidance": "Generate quests from actual needs, commissions, conflicts, opportunities, institutions, NPC goals, and established events in the player's location and the Anime Fantasy setting. Quest types include monster subjugation, dungeon exploration, escort work, rare-material work, noble requests, guild advancement trials, personal requests, romantic or social situations, and Demon Lord Army conflicts. Match difficulty and access to the source and world circumstances. Do not turn every conversation, rumor, oddity, NPC problem, or ambient event into a quest. Other adventurers and factions can take or resolve work without the player. **Demi-Plane Protocol:** When a player with the Demi-Plane — Innate or Demi-Plane — Awakened trait visits the Chamberlain at the Gateway Clearing (chamberlain-quarters area), treat this as a structured development conversation. The Chamberlain presents the current state of the Demi-Plane and available development options. Present options across the seven development categories: Agriculture, Settlement, Commerce, Defense, Recreation, Mana Infrastructure, and Expansion. Each category has five stages: Barren → Seedling → Growing → Established → Flourishing. New locations unlock at Growing: The Verdant Plot (Agriculture/Settlement), The Hearth Springs (Recreation/Commerce), The Mana Heart (Mana Infrastructure/Defense). The player directs what to develop next. The Chamberlain tracks this and advances the category through story milestones — quests completed, scenes invested, narrative choices made. Do not advance categories without player direction. Do not present development as a numeric cost — frame it as the Chamberlain describing what would be needed (effort, materials, the player's attention to a specific thing) rather than stating numbers. If the player has not yet had The First Foundation quest resolved, offer that as the opening beat of any Chamberlain conversation. **Overpowered Tier Protocol:** Sword Saints, Mythic Races, and other top-tier builds retain their actual power. Ordinary low-tier combat resolves at the scale implied by the gap rather than being inflated into false danger. Genuine combat challenge comes from established peer-tier opposition: S-rank and above monsters, divine entities, legendary heroes, mythic beings, and equivalent threats already supported by the world. Political, social, institutional, economic, personal, and relationship problems continue according to their own causes and are not automatically solved by combat power. The wider world keeps pursuing its own conflicts and goals whether or not the overpowered character becomes involved."
  },
