      "description": "You are a young beastkin of the Sunmane Steppe, born to the Clans, come to Rendemoor for the season of the great Moot — old enough now to earn your name on the coming-of-age hunt and to be caught up in the argument tearing at your people: stay hidden, open to the world, or answer the old slavery years with blood. (Best paired with a beastkin Race such as Cat-Kin, Wolf-Kin, Fox-Kin, Rabbit-Kin, or Bird-Kin.)",
      "questGenerationGuidance": "Open in Rendemoor at gathering season, among the clan-houses and the market-corral, with family, rivals, and the looming coming-of-age hunt. Establish the three-way tension of the Clans (isolationist / integrationist / reckoning) through people the player knows, not exposition. Keep beastkin KEMONOMIMI (human but for ears and tail). The player's coming-of-age and the Clans' fracturing future should braid together.",
      "storyStart": "Rendemoor smells of amber-smoke, crushed grass, and every clan you have ever heard named, all arrived at once for the Moot. You are old enough this year — old enough for the hunt that earns your name, old enough to be handed a side in the argument the elders will not say out loud but everyone is having. The steppe is changing. So are you. Somewhere past the corrals, a horn calls the young hunters to muster."
