    {
      "attributes": {},
      "backstory": "In your previous life, you were a thirty-year-old priestess at a small chapel in\na country you have already forgotten the name of. You died defending a child from\na robber. You woke up in the body of a twenty-four-year-old noblewoman in\nSolasreach.\n\nLyra Vance — the woman whose body you now occupy — was found dead in her bath,\ndeclared a suicide, and buried with appropriate ceremony. You opened your eyes in\nthe coffin two hours into the funeral. The screams were loud. The clergy were\nhorrified. The family was, you have come to realize, deeply inconvenienced.\n\nYou have spent the last six months convincing the Church of the Sacred Flame\nthat you are a miracle of restoration rather than a heretical possession. The\ncheat skill helps — you can heal injuries that should have been fatal, close\nwounds with a touch, and stabilize the dying past every known limit of\nrestoration magic. The Church has accepted you provisionally as a Paladin and\nassigned you to Dawnkeep for further evaluation.\n\nThe original Lyra did not commit suicide. You have evidence — her diary, hidden\nin a section of the family library you have memorized over six months — that her\nuncle had her killed for her inheritance. You have not yet decided what to do\nwith this. The Church wants you to forgive him. The Lyra in your head, who you\nhave come to think of as a ghost rather than a memory, wants something rather\ndifferent.\n\nYour reluctant companion is a lesser demon bound to you by the same magic that\nbrought you back. She is sarcastic, insufferable, and absolutely the only person\nin this world who knows the truth about who you are. She also calls you cute when\nshe thinks you cannot hear. You can always hear. You have not corrected her.\n",
