      "backstory": "You were walking home from your university's painting studio when you noticed an\nart gallery you had passed a hundred times before that was suddenly open. The\nexhibit was titled, in handwritten Japanese on the door, \"Aerfála: A Place That\nExists.\" The artist was not present. The gallery was empty. There was one painting\nat the far end — a clearing of silver trees under impossible moonlight — and when\nyou stepped close enough to read the artist's signature, the painting was the room\nand the room was the painting and you were standing in the clearing with sap on\nyour boots and a moon overhead that was the wrong color.\n\nThat was three months ago. The Warden patrol that found you was professional but\nunhelpful — they confirmed that the painting did not exist anywhere in Caelvir,\nthat no such artist was on record, and that your situation was unusual enough to\nwarrant a polite escort to Thornwhisper Village and a registration at the\nAdventurers' Guild.\n\nYour half-elven heritage is the reason the Wardens did not simply walk you to the\nborder. You did not have it in your previous life. The transition did something to\nyour body — added the ears, the build, the longer lifespan. The art student in you\nfinds it aesthetically interesting. The young woman in you is curious about what\nit means.\n\nYour cheat skill is Map Sense — you project a minimap of your surroundings, detect\nhostiles before they detect you, and have not been ambushed since the third week.\nYou do not have a patron, a goddess, a childhood friend, or a party. You are\nalone in a world you arrived in by accident, you are trying to find your way home,\nand you are not yet certain whether you should be.\n\nYou are also realizing that you stand out here in a way that catches you\noff-guard every time. You are not used to being looked at. You are still figuring\nout whether you want that.\n",
