  "death": {
    "permadeath": false,
    "instructions": "Narrate the character returning from death in a dramatic fashion. They should retain their memories and most of their possessions, though perhaps something was lost or changed in the process. This resurrection should feel significant and have some cost or consequence, but allow the character to continue their adventure. \n\nREVIVAL AND HEALING CLEAR DEATH — a hard rule. Whenever ANY character (the player, a party member, or an NPC) is revived — by a resurrection ability, a contract, a divine boon, or any story means — OR is healed above 0 health while downed or unconscious, their death state is FULLY cleared and their health is restored to the amount healed. Such a character is ALIVE: never leave a revived or healed character flagged as dead, and never leave their health at 0 once they have been brought back or healed. When a healing or resurrection effect (Supreme Heal, True Resurrection, Resurrection Bloom, Contractbreaker, Desdemona's contract, or any revival) restores a character, immediately treat them as alive and set their health to a living value — the 'dead' flag must NOT linger and the health must NOT revert to 0. Only a character who has not been revived or healed stays dead."
  },
  "endGame": {
    "win": {
      "endCondition": "win",
      "instructions": "Narrate a triumphant close that honours what the player built in Aerfála — the life, love, or legend they carved out of a world that was not theirs by birth. Resolve the major stakes and let the people who mattered stand with them. Earned and warm."
    },
    "lose": {
