'd rather you see it yourself than take my word.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> She starts up the lane without waiting, her steady stride carrying her past the garden gates toward the north edge of the village. The morning sun catches the grey in her braid.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hazel> Hazel tugs Sorrel and Campion back a step by their collars, pulling them into a huddle. Her voice drops to a fierce whisper that carries perfectly across the quiet lane.\n\nHazel: [whispering] She's going to walk the north wall with Brynja. I'm going to watch the whole time. If anything comes back, I'll see it first.",
