      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You turn from the well plot and move to Hazel's position in three quick strides, dropping to a crouch beside her at the hedge line. Your eyes follow her gaze to the treeline where the north path disappears into shadow.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You scan the tree line the way you scan a battlefield — not looking for shapes, but for breaks in pattern. The morning light falls unevenly through the canopy, casting bars of shadow between the trunks. Most of them hold still. One does not. A patch of shadow at the path's mouth shifts left when the wind blows right, and the branch above it doesn't sway with its neighbors. Something is crouching behind the third trunk from the gap — low, compact, holding still with the practiced patience of something that has done this before. The shape is too wide for a fox, too short for a person.",
        "Hazel: [barely audible] It moved again. Left side. Behind the big tree.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Hazel> Hazel creeps forward two steps along the hedge, pressing herself against the low branches to angle her sight line past the gatepost. Her ears stay flat. Her tail is wrapped tight around her own ankle.",
        "Brynja: [calling] Tsukiko — come feel this. The roots are drinking straight from the well. If it sinks another hand's width, the water's done.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja doesn't look up. Her fingers dig deeper into the furrow, following a blackened root thread down toward the water line, her jaw set and her grey tail bristling along its length."
      ],
