      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I praise Hazel and tell her to ignore it and act as if she gave up looking. Not because we do give up, but to set a small trap and invite whoever, or whatever, there is to make a mistake. Then i go back to brynja to help her fix the issue."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] Good eyes, Hazel. Now do something for me. Stop watching. Drop the braid, stand up, stretch — like you got bored and gave up. Turn around and walk back toward the village. Not fast. Not slow. Just a kit who lost interest.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hazel> Hazel's ears swivel toward you, both flat, her amber eyes wide. Her mouth opens — then closes. She looks back at the treeline, back at you, and something clicks behind her eyes. She shoves the grass braid into her pocket, stands, stretches her arms above her head with exaggerated laziness, and yawns loud enough to carry.\n\nHazel: [loudly, performative] There's nothing out here. I'm going back.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hazel> She turns and saunters down the lane toward the village-green, bare feet slapping the packed earth. Her tail swings loose and easy. Her ears — still flat — track backward the entire way, swiveling independently, listening for anything behind her she can no longer see.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You leave the hedge and walk back to Brynja at the well plot, your stride unhurried, your naginata still resting across your back. To anything watching from the trees, you are a woman returning to her work.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja's fingers are buried wrist-deep in the furrow, following a blackened root thread that vanishes into the dark soil toward the well's stone base. She doesn't look up when you crouch beside her.\n\nBrynja: [gruffly] Feel here. The root runs straight down — it's drinking from the well water before it reaches the surface. Two more hands' width and it's in the stone.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You press your fingers into the furrow beside hers. The root thread is warm and slick under the soil, pulsing faintly with the same sluggish sourness you felt in the Ashfords' plot — but thicker here, denser, fed by the well's steady moisture. It traces a crooked line straight down toward the water table, branching into hair-thin veins that spread through the surrounding earth like cracks in old ice.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] I feel it. The root is drawing the taint straight from the water. We need to break the thread and flood the furrow before it reaches the well stone. Turn the soil here — I will guide your hands to where the roots branch.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja pulls the hoe from where she drove it and hands it to you handle-first without a word, already scraping at the earth with her bare hands to expose the main root thread where it thickens near the well's foundation.",
