      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You keep your hands in the furrow, fingers working the broken root threads aside, clearing the trench so the dark fluid drains into the open soil instead of seeping downward. Your ears track the treeline behind you — but your eyes stay on the earth, your posture bent and busy, a woman absorbed in her work.",
        "Brynja: [gruffly, without looking up] There's a rain barrel behind my shed — thirty paces south. The water's clean. We flood the furrow with that, not the well. If we pour tainted water back on this, we've done nothing.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja's hands keep moving, scraping soil away from the broken root ends, her knuckles black with the foul sap. She doesn't glance toward the trees. She doesn't need to — her grey ears are angled backward, rigid, tracking something she hasn't named yet.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Duskmaw> The shadow at the treeline slides forward another half-step. Its belly presses flat to the ground, claws finding purchase in the loose leaf litter, pale eyes unblinking as it measures the gap between the hedge's end and the nearest garden wall. The two figures at the well haven't moved. The smaller one that was watching is gone. It edges closer."
      ],
