      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I gently stop Brynja's knife hand and raise my other to about chest hight, index finger softly extended upwards and one little flame at it's tip \"Brynja, please be mindful. Wounds heal. Blood is messy. So if you'd let me handle this please?\" Then i look at the creature \"Since i'm a patient person i'll ask you again to explain yourself. If you try to flee or make me repeat myself again? Well.. patience has it's limits and, in case you didn't know, souls can burn too.\""
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You reach out and close your fingers gently around Brynja's knife hand — not gripping, just resting, the way you'd still a trembling teacup. Your other hand rises to chest height, index finger extended, and a single foxfire flame blooms at its tip, small and steady as a votive candle.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] Brynja, please be mindful. Wounds heal. Blood is messy. So if you'd let me handle this please?\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja's grey eyes drop to the flame on your fingertip, then back to your face. Her jaw works once — then she eases the knife back into its sheath with a deliberate click. She doesn't step back. She plants her boots between the trench and the village green, shoulders squared, one hand still resting on the sheath.\n\nBrynja: [low] All yours.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You turn your gaze to the creature in the flooded furrow. The foxfire on your fingertip doesn't flicker.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] Since I'm a patient person I'll ask you again to explain yourself. If you try to flee or make me repeat myself again? Well... patience has its limits and, in case you didn't know, souls can burn too.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Duskmaw> The scrabbling stops. The creature's claws sink slowly into the mud, and its haunches lower until its belly rests in the flooded furrow. A low, rattling hiss pushes through its throat — not a snarl, not a warning. Its pale eyes drop from the glowing markings to the mud beneath it, and the wedge-shaped head lowers until it is nearly flat against the ground. The sound trails off into silence. It is waiting.",
