        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I smile warmly, sincerely, and explain to it that i do not seek it's life, the miko in me taking lead."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You shift your weight in the mud, silk dragging in the furrow water, and your face opens — not a performance, not a mask of mercy, but the real thing. The warmth reaches your eyes first, then your mouth, then the set of your shoulders as they ease. Your palm stays on the creature's coarse, cold skull.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly, in the Old Tongue] I don't seek your life. That isn't why I'm here. You were used by something that promised you safety it never intended to deliver — I understand that. So give me everything, and I give you my word: you will walk away from this furrow alive. That's not mercy I'm offering. It's simply what I am.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Duskmaw> The creature's pale eyes fix on your face. Its throat works once — a dry, clicking swallow — and the tension in its haunches bleeds out by degrees, muscle by muscle, until its belly settles fully into the mud. Something in its posture shifts. Not trust, exactly. Recognition that the hand on its head is not going to close.\n\nDuskmaw: [guttural, rapid] *Three places. The well — you found that one. The hollow beneath the Ashford wall — roots run deep there, deepest of all, the dark ones spoke loudest through it. And the north stream, where it bends past the old stones. The water turns black there at night. I did not make it black. I only... tended.*\n\nNarrator: <focus:Duskmaw> Its claws curl once in the mud, then flatten.\n\nDuskmaw: [low, broken] *The larger thing — the dark ones said it comes from the east. Where the ground is already soft. Where the wards are old. They did not say what it is. They said: when the roots reach the well, the place is ready. Then we go. We are small. We are not... for the larger thing. We are for the tending.*\n\nNarrator: <focus:Duskmaw> A long, shuddering breath. Its pale eyes drift to the treeline, then back.\n\nDuskmaw: [quiet] *That is everything. Every sound. Every dark place. May I go now, keeper?*\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja steps forward, her boots grinding into the mud, and stops a pace behind your shoulder. Her grey ears are flat, her eyes fixed on the creature's lowered head. She speaks low, not quite a whisper, pitched only for you.\n\nBrynja: [low, firm] I heard your tone even if I can't hear the words. Can it be trusted? And if you let it walk — is this village actually safe, or just quiet until the next thing crawls out of those roots?",
