      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I look at tom \"interesting words considering what you know as miko is not what i was taught a miko is so your assumption is rather.. loose. But so be it.\" I finish my tea, pay and leave to check the last spot the burrower mentioned."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [mildly, setting down her cup] Interesting words, considering your notion of what a miko is isn't what I was taught a miko is. Your assumption is rather... loose. But so be it.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You finish the tea in one unhurried swallow, set coins on the bar — exact, counted — and rise, taking up your naginata.\n\nOld Tom Hedley: [dry] Loose it may be. Forty years of ledgers doesn't make me a scholar. Safe travels, miko.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja steps fully inside as you pass, dropping her voice and cutting straight past greeting.\n\nBrynja: [low, urgent] Before you go — the stone under the wall is old. Older than the wall built over it, by the look of the cut. Whatever's etched on it isn't any script I've seen in this valley. You saw it once already, near the well root. Do you recognize the markings? I'd rather you tell me before half the village comes gawking.\n\nNarrator: <arrival> You leave the Wagging Tail and walk out past the garden rows into the outskirts, where the fields give way to rough grass and the orchards thin toward wilder ground. The ley-spring bubbles quietly at the center of the plots, its water clear and warm, steam curling off it in the morning air — and here, close to the trees, the ground is softer, pocked and ridged.",
