      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You lean closer to the aperture, your eyes narrowing as you trace the flowing ritual cypher. To a mortal scholar, this would be a lifetime of study, but your awareness pierces the basalt like sunlight through glass. You recognize the logic of the binding—it is a weight-anchor, designed to compress the volatile ley-energy into a manageable spring rather than a destructive eruption.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You detect the hairline fractures within the stone’s internal mana-lattice; the goblin hex acted like acid, eating at the spiritual integrity of the seal. It is a masterpiece of ancient engineering, yet it is brittle now, vibrating with a frequency that suggests it is struggling to contain the surge of the deep earth.",
        "Brynja: [hesitant] You’re looking at it the way a smith looks at a cracked anvil. Is it... is it dying?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You remain silent, considering the truth of the situation. The seal is not dying, but it is overtaxed; it was never meant to filter corruption, only to hold pressure. Fixing it requires more than simple masonry—it requires a re-tuning of the ley-line's own resonance to match the stone's original song.",
        "Brynja: [firmly] Tell me what you need, miko. If I have to dig out this entire section of the wall by hand, I’ll do it. Or if there’s some herb, some metal we need to fetch from Tom’s stores...",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja shifts her weight, her tail twitching with restless energy as she looks from the stone to the distant well. Her hands, stained with the soil of a lifetime’s labor, clench into fists at her sides.",
        "Brynja: [low] I won't just stand here and watch the water turn to rot while the children are sleeping. There has to be a way to brace it. Just tell me where to put my strength."
      ],
