      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] Your strength is already where it needs to be, Brynja. The land knows you. It is your hands that have fed it, and it is that connection we must use to steady this stone.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You extend your hand, the jade ring on your finger catching the morning light as you hover your palm over the basalt slab. The heat rising from the hollow intensifies, a low thrumming that begins to vibrate through the soles of your sandals. You can see the mana-lattice clearly now—it is a tangled, dissonant web of static where it should be a clear, melodic flow.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] I do not need silver or herbs. I need you to anchor the physical world while I speak to the spirit of this place.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja nods, her expression hardening into a mask of grim determination. She drops to one knee beside you, her thick tail sweeping the grass as she braces her calloused hands against the foundational stones of the wall, pressing her weight into the earth as if to hold the very village in place.\n\nBrynja: [firmly] I’m here. I’m holding. Tell me if I need to move a stone, or if there’s a tool at the forge that can bite into this work. Just guide me.\n\nTsukiko Kuzunoha: [gently] No tools. Only your presence. When the stone begins to shift its song, it will feel like the ground is trying to pull away from you. Do not let go of the wall.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You close your eyes, letting your awareness expand beyond the physical outskirts. The bioluminescent markings on your skin begin to pulse with a soft, rhythmic light—a steady heartbeat that contrasts with the erratic, jagged vibration of the ley-seal. You reach into the Item Box of your mind, drawing forth the resonance of the Mother Fox to meet the ancient, struggling mechanism.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> The air around the hollow begins to hum, and the steam rising from the ley-spring in the distance turns a faint, shimmering gold. Brynja’s ears twitch violently as the stone beneath her hands let out a low, metallic groan, the carved script beginning to glow with a dull, sunset orange.\n\nBrynja: [gasping] It’s... it’s moving! The heat is coming up through my boots, miko! Is this the re-tuning? Is it working?",
