      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> The silver-white brilliance of your markings recedes, leaving only the soft, ambient morning light and the revitalized basalt seal. The jagged, angry orange heat has vanished, replaced by a deep, cool resonance that feels like a heavy heart finally finding its rhythm. The flowing script on the stone has settled into a perfect, frozen geometry, humming with a quiet power that signifies the ley-line's stabilization.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja slowly exhales, her shoulders dropping as the violent vibrations beneath her palms finally cease. She holds her position for a moment longer, testing the silence of the earth, before she eases the pressure and pulls her hands away from the foundational stones.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> She stands up with a stiff, weary grace, her boots squelching slightly in the churned marl. Wiping her soil-stained hands onto her apron with shaking fingers, she looks down at the basalt slab, then back at you with a mixture of physical exhaustion and genuine, wide-eyed awe.",
        "Brynja: [breathless] It’s quiet. Even the wind feels different. It’s like the whole village just... stopped holding its breath.",
        "Brynja: [softly] I’ve lived here all my life, miko. I’ve seen the spring bubble and the harvests come and go, but I never knew we were sitting on something so... so heavy.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> She reaches up to adjust her silver-streaked braid, her ears twitching as they catch the distant, cheerful sound of a dinner bell from the village green. The tension that has gripped her since the garden first blackened seems to dissolve, leaving her looking older, but infinitely more at peace.",
        "Brynja: [warmly] You didn’t just fix a stone. You saved our home. I think... I think Tom was right to be quiet about you. People around here aren't used to miracles that actually work."
      ],
