 common-house folk begin to treat your word as sacred law, not out of fear, but because of the undeniable prosperity that follows your footsteps. Even the most cynical farmers find themselves speaking more softly to their livestock, influenced by the magnetic, tranquil authority you project.\n\nBrynja: [warmly] Look at them, miko. They aren't just farming anymore. They're... they're honoring it. I think even the Ashfords are starting to believe the ground loves them back.",
