      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [calmly] When you till the soil tomorrow, Brynja, do not think of it as breaking the earth. Think of it as opening a window for the ground to breathe. If you move with the weight of the tool rather than fighting against it, the land will meet you halfway.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You pause by the edge of the Ashford plot, smoothing the front of your pristine vestments. Your bioluminescent markings give off a faint, contented silver pulse, mirroring the renewed vitality of the nearby sprouts. You offer a few more quiet insights on how to read the ripening rhythm of the fruit trees before beginning to turn back toward the village center.",
        "Brynja: [warmly] Open a window... I’ll keep that in my mind, miko. It’s a kinder way to look at a day’s labor.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja gives you a final, supportive nod, her silver-and-ash braid swinging as she looks out over the thriving greenery. She wipes a smudge of healthy, damp earth from her cheek, her expression softening into one of deep, earned respect.",
        "Brynja: [firmly] Be careful on the path back, even if it is a short walk. The village feels safe, but the Marches have long memories. Mira is likely waiting for you at the common-house with a fresh pot of tea—I’d not keep her waiting, or the brew will go bitter.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> She glances over her shoulder toward the village green, where the distant, high-pitched laughter of the Rabbit-Kin kits carries on the afternoon breeze. Her ears twitch with a protective alertness as she watches Hazel chasing Sorrel through a patch of tall grass.",
        "Brynja: [softly] I’ll stay here and keep an eye on the little ones while you're gone. They’re so full of your light today, I doubt they’ll want to come inside until the moon is up. Go on, now. You’ve done more than enough for one afternoon."
      ],
