      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Brynja> Brynja watches you for a heartbeat longer, her expression holding a quiet, maternal warmth that seems to have replaced her old defensive sharpness. She raises a calloused hand in a final, encouraging wave, the grey fur on her arm catching the golden afternoon light.\n\nBrynja: [warmly] Go on, miko. We'll be right here when the shadows grow long.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Brynja> She turns her back to the path and steps toward the center of the Ashford plot, her tail swaying with a relaxed rhythm. She moves with a new lightness, closing the distance to the children to ensure their play remains within the safety of the revitalized garden.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hazel> In the tall grass, Hazel skids to a halt, her ears perking up as she senses your departure. She abandons her pursuit of the giggling Rabbit-Kin kits and spins around, her amber eyes locking onto your silhouette with fierce, childhood devotion.\n\nHazel: [shouting] Bye, Lady Tsukiko! Come back soon!\n\nNarrator: <focus:Hazel> She waves her small hand enthusiastically, her expressive tail lashing back and forth in a blur of grey tabby fur. Her smile is wide and beaming, radiating the uncomplicated joy of a child who finally feels the world is a kind place.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> The distant laughter of Sorrel and Campion rises like birdcall behind you as you begin the short walk back toward the village green. The air in the outskirts is heavy with the scent of wild roses and damp, healthy earth, the malevolent chill of the goblin hex now nothing more than a fading memory.\n\nNarrator: The packed-earth track feels firm and welcoming beneath your feet, leading you away from the vibrant orchards toward the heart of Whiskerbrook. As the outskirts fall behind, the quiet hum of the common-house and the craft-quarter grows louder, signaling the end of a long, prosperous day of tending the world's mirror.",
