      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Mira Thistledown> Mira leans forward, her elbows resting on the table as she hitches her chair closer to yours. Her long rabbit ears tilt forward in rapt attention, and she rests her chin on her palms, her eyes wide and shining with the dreamy fascination of a child hearing a fairy tale.",
        "Mira Thistledown: [whispering] Trees with memories... oh, Lady Tsukiko, that sounds so beautiful. Do they speak to you in whispers when the wind catches them, or do they show what they've seen in the way their leaves turn color in the autumn?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Old Tom Hedley> Old Tom lets out a deep hum of interest, his gaze drifting for a moment as if he’s trying to picture such a place. He reaches for a ceramic jug behind the bar and pours himself a modest measure of golden cider, the liquid catching the firelight as it swirls into his mug.",
        "Old Tom Hedley: [thoughtfully] A land where the silence isn't empty. I’ve spent many a night in the deep woods, and I can tell you, most silence has teeth out here in the Marches. It’s rare to find a place that feels like it’s actually watching over you.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Old Tom Hedley> He takes a slow, appreciative sip of his cider, letting the sharpness of the apple settle before he wipes his mouth with the back of a calloused hand. He looks back at you, a spark of old-world curiosity in his eyes.",
        "Old Tom Hedley: [jovial] It makes me wonder about the folk who live alongside those trees. Are the spirits of your land as fond of a good drink and a long tale as the ones I’ve heard of in the old songs? Or are they the sort who prefer to be left to their brooding?",
        "Narrator: <focus:Mira Thistledown> Mira doesn't look away from you, her nose twitching rhythmically as she waits for your answer. The bustling energy she usually carries has settled into a quiet, intense focus, as if she’s trying to catch the scent of that distant, magical forest on your very robes.",
        "Mira Thistledown: [softly] I think I would like a forest that remembers. It makes the world feel less... less lonely, knowing the ground knows you were there. Is that why you’re so kind to our soil, Lady Tsukiko? Because you know it’s listening?"
      ],
