      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You keep your answers drifting — a far country, past the Marches, past the remembered trees — close enough to be real, vague enough to never point at a torii. You sip the tea and let the warmth carry the stories.",
        "Mira Thistledown: [wistful] I've always wondered if there are places like that, where the heart can truly be at peace. Is your homeland one of them, Lady Tsukiko? A place where one could simply stop... and belong, without fear?",
        "Old Tom Hedley: [warmly] Fine tonic, these stories of yours. Just what a man needs before a long winter. And speaking of belonging — the Wagging Tail's got room, and I'll knock a fair bit off the rate if you'd stay on a few more nights. Village would be honored to have a miko under its roof a while longer.",
        "Mira Thistledown: [softly] Oh — please say yes! The kits would be so happy, and Brynja too, though she'd never admit it out loud.",
        "Old Tom Hedley: [chuckling] No pressure, mind. But the offer stands as long as the hearth's burning."
      ],
