      "playerInputs": {
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha": "I tilt my head softly in consideration, thinking. I have no concrete plans or a destination. So a few more days might not hurt if the villagers wish for it. Hm.. but i also can't just remain here.. so just a few days more.. maybe, if they wish, i could even relocate their village to my realm.. hmm.. worth a thought."
      },
      "storyMessage": "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [softly] Hm... a few more days might not hurt, if the village wishes it. I have no pressing road ahead of me — only thoughts that wander.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Mira Thistledown> Mira's whole face lights up. She clasps her hands together and nearly rises out of her chair, ears standing tall with delight.\n\nMira Thistledown: [cheerful] Oh, wonderful! If you stay, I'll prepare a proper feast for the whole village — a real celebration, with pies and roasted roots and everything! The kits will talk about it for seasons!\n\nNarrator: <focus:Old Tom Hedley> Old Tom leans back with a long, contented sigh, his chair groaning as he folds his hands over his belly.\n\nOld Tom Hedley: [calmly] No rush here, miko. The cider stays cold and the fire stays warm whether you decide tomorrow or next week. Take your time — the Marches aren't going anywhere, and neither are we.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You let the thought drift where it wants — a whole village, roots and hearths and rabbit-eared children, carried gently into your own quiet world. The idea settles in your chest like a warm coal, worth turning over later. For now, you only smile into your tea.\n\nMira Thistledown: [softly] You look like you're thinking about something lovely, Lady Tsukiko. I can always tell — your eyes go all warm.\n\nOld Tom Hedley: [chuckling] Aye, and whatever it is, I'll wager it involves feeding people. That's the mark of a good heart, or a very clever innkeeper.",
