      "storyParagraphs": [
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You finish the last of your tea and toast, rising with a small bow toward the bar.",
        "Tsukiko Kuzunoha: [warmly] Thank you for the breakfast, Hedley. The tea was perfect as ever.",
        "Old Tom Hedley: [gruffly] Save the thanks for after you survive Mira's morning. Off with you.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Mira Thistledown> Mira is already halfway out the door, bunting coil bobbing. She leads you across the green to the first wooden post, one hand sketching the air as she talks.",
        "Mira Thistledown: [briskly] Here — the string goes from this post to the big oak, and it has to sag just so, see? A gentle dip, like a smile. That way the bunting frames the hills instead of hiding them. Mother always said the hills are the village's finest decoration, and I refuse to cover them up.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Tsukiko Kuzunoha> You take your end and walk it to the oak, matching her pace. The string comes taut between you, and Mira darts along it, pinning autumn-colored cloth at intervals with practiced little jabs.",
        "Mira Thistledown: [cheerful] Perfect! Oh, you have a natural touch — not a single crook in it. The kits will be so impressed.",
        "Narrator: <focus:Ashford brother 1> Across the green, the Ashford brothers wrestle the cider barrel over the uneven turf. The older one braces a shoulder against it, boots skidding in the grass.",
        "Ashford brother 1: [straining] Winston, push! Lean into it — it's fighting us like a live pig!",
        "Ashford brother 2: [gasping] I am pushing! This thing weighs more than the house!",
        "Narrator: <focus:Ashford brother 1> The barrel lurches, tips, and rolls free of both brothers, thundering across the green in a wobbling line — straight toward the stream that cuts through the Brook-Green."
      ],
