      "storyMessage": "Narrator: The barrel gathers speed, bouncing over the turf, its rim throwing off sparks of morning light as it races for the water.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ashford brother 1> The older Ashford tears after it, boots hammering the grass. He shouts a warning, arms stretched wide, fingers grazing the rolling rim as he throws his whole weight into the catch.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ashford brother 2> The younger one yelps, trips over his own feet, and sprawls flat in the grass. He scrambles up a heartbeat later and sprints after his brother, arms pumping.\n\nMira Thistledown: [shouting] Not the cider!\n\nNarrator: <focus:Mira Thistledown> Mira drops her end of the bunting in a heap and takes off toward the stream, skirts gathered in both fists, ears snapping fully upright.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Ashford brother 1> The older brother's palms slap the barrel's rim — and the momentum carries him forward, boots skidding on the wet bank. He hugs the cask to his chest, heels digging twin furrows, and grinds it to a shuddering stop a hand's width from the water's edge.\n\nAshford brother 1: [wheezing] Got it — I've got it — somebody tell my arms they still work.\n\nAshford brother 2: [laughing breathlessly] Kaelen, you absolute ox, you caught it with your face half a second from drowning in the brook!\n\nMira Thistledown: [panting, relieved] Oh thank the harvest — Kaelen, are you all right? Winston, help him roll it back before his grip gives out!",
