      "storyMessage": "Narrator: <focus:Kaelen Ashford> The brothers each grab a side of the barrel and heave it upright together, boots braced against the turf.\n\nWinston Ashford: [loudly, to the green] Cider's safe! Nobody drowned, nobody's wine is soup — carry on!\n\nNarrator: <focus:Winston Ashford> He gives the cask a triumphant shove, and the two of them roll it bumping toward the tasting tables.\n\nWinston Ashford: [teasing] You know what I saw, Kaelen? A grown man hugging a barrel like it owed him money.\n\nKaelen Ashford: [flatly] I saw you eating grass, Winston. We all saw it.\n\nNarrator: <focus:Mira Thistledown> Mira steers you back across the green to a long trestle crowded with buckets and baskets — sunflowers, marigolds, late roses, bundles of wheat tied with ribbon.\n\nMira Thistledown: [briskly] Now — these are what the village grew this year, so every bloom gets its moment. The marigolds go along the table edges, wheat for the arch. But the lilies, oh, the lilies are the pride of it. My opinion's worn out from staring at them. Where would you put them for the most striking show?",
